                    <occupation>OCCUPATION</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Ed Pope writes: The letter of 9.9.1806 John P Binham to Godwin from 1,
                            Evesham Buildings (Bodl MS Abinger c.10 f.4) mentioned his temporary
                            engagement with Mr Phillips (presumably the publisher Richard Phillips).
                            John Pearson Binham son of Richard and Esther his wife born 20.7.1771
                            (Quaker Devon East Division). John Binham [married at St] Pancras 5.7.1807 Maria
                            Ballanger. Elizabeth born 24.11.1807 at Somers Town to John Pearson
                            Binham and Maria wits at birth Ann Ballanger, Mary Ann Lovell, Esther
                            Maria born 15.8.1812 at Somers Town of same parents wits Mary Ann
                            Townsend, Louisa Ballanger (Quaker London and Middlesex meeting - not a
                            member). 1841 census 30 Wych St John Binham accountant age 65. John
                            Pearson Binham bur 15.5.1847 age 76 St Dunstan i t West</p>
                    </note>
